        <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--paper" id="applications">
            <div class="commercial-shell">
                <div class="commercial-heading commercial-heading--split">
                    <div>
                        <p class="commercial-overline">Commercial applications</p>
                        <h2>Different buildings. Different glass decisions.</h2>
                    </div>
                    <p>Film selection starts with how the space is used, who sees through the glass, where the sun
                        lands, and what access the project requires.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="commercial-property-grid">
                    <article><span>01</span><h3>Offices</h3><p>Exterior glazing, conference rooms, interior partitions, and shared work areas.</p></article>
                    <article><span>02</span><h3>Storefronts + restaurants</h3><p>Customer-facing glass, street exposure, display areas, and entry doors.</p></article>
                    <article><span>03</span><h3>Hospitality + healthcare</h3><p>Guest, patient, staff, and service spaces with distinct privacy and light needs.</p></article>
                    <article><span>04</span><h3>Multi-family common areas</h3><p>Lobbies, amenity rooms, management offices, and other shared commercial glass.</p></article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--ink" id="solutions">
            <div class="commercial-shell">
                <div class="commercial-heading">
                    <p class="commercial-overline">Film solutions</p>
                    <h2>Define the outcome before choosing the film.</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="commercial-solution-list">
                    <article><p class="commercial-solution-list__number">01 / Climate</p><h3>Solar, heat + glare</h3><p>Review film options intended to manage sun-exposed glass, screen glare, and uneven comfort while considering the existing glazing.</p></article>
                    <article><p class="commercial-solution-list__number">02 / Visibility</p><h3>Privacy + decorative film</h3><p>Explore frosted, patterned, and visibility-control applications for customer, staff, meeting, and interior glass.</p></article>
                    <article><p class="commercial-solution-list__number">03 / Glass retention</p><h3>Safety + security film</h3><p>Discuss the site, glass, attachment approach, and project intent before identifying an appropriate system.</p></article>
                    <article><p class="commercial-solution-list__number">04 / Exposure</p><h3>UV + fade considerations</h3><p>Review sun exposure around furnishings, finishes, displays, and occupied areas without promising elimination of fading.</p></article>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="commercial-section commercial-section--image" id="privacy-decorative">
            <div class="commercial-shell commercial-image-callout">
